# The number SockSock_Errno answers is the host's (`docs/design/decisions.md`): ENOTCONN is 107
# on Linux and 57 on macOS.
# SockSock_Errno: a failing call's errno; a success leaves it, and a host
# lookup sets it to 0 first. Before any call it is 0 (Rulings, errno: the
# oracle reports the errno its own console I/O left).
ruled
say SockSock_Errno()
call SockShutDown 9999, 2
say SockSock_Errno()
call SockVersion
say SockSock_Errno()
c = SockSocket('AF_INET', 'SOCK_STREAM', '0')
call SockShutDown c, 2
say SockSock_Errno()
call SockIoctl c, 'FIONBIO', 0
say SockSock_Errno()
call SockGetHostByName '127.1', 'h.'
say SockSock_Errno()
::requires 'rxsock' LIBRARY
----
rc 0
[stdout]
0
9
9
107
107
0
[stderr]
